// Combustion and the Smagorinsky strain closure in one dispatch.
//
// The two stages are independent: combustion is cell-local on the scalar pair,
// strain reads the velocity faces and writes nu_t, and neither reads what the
// other writes. Merging them is therefore not an approximation — it is the same
// two bodies in the same order, one workgroup launch and one barrier fewer.
//
// The order below is the point of the merge, not an accident. strain's 11^3
// velocity cache is 3993 loads that combustion does not need, and combustion is
// the solver's only transcendental-heavy stage (an exp and two pow per cell), so
// the cache fill is issued first and combustion's arithmetic runs while it is in
// flight. The barrier that publishes the cache sits between them, which is why
// combustion_body must not contain one: it returns early on out-of-grid cells and
// a barrier it skipped would not be workgroup-uniform.
//
// The sources of both stages are concatenated ahead of this file by
// FireGpuSolver, which compiles them with FIRE_MERGED so their standalone mains
// are left out.

void main() {
	ivec3 c = cell_coord();
	strain_prefetch();
	combustion_body(c);
	barrier();
	strain_body(c);
}
